<!--
    Bridge animals for Le Mechet map (FS25_The_Mechet) by MA7Studio.

    The map adds four French cow breeds with custom 3D models:
      - COW_CHAROLAISE   (heavy beef; visualAnimalIndex 19/20/21 = adult/kid/baby)
      - COW_MONTBELIARDE (PDO Comte dairy; visualAnimalIndex 22/23/24)
      - COW_SIMMENTAL    (dual-purpose Fleckvieh; visualAnimalIndex 25/26/27)
      - COW_VOSGIENNE    (small mountain dairy; visualAnimalIndex 28/29/30)

    The map registers these subtypes in maps/animals/animals.xml at lines 500/579/663/747.
    The custom 3D models live in maps/animals/cow/{CharolaiseEtSimmental,MontbeliardeEtVosgienne}/
    referenced from maps/animals/cow/animals.xml at indices 19-30 (note: 1-based).

    This bridge file:

      1. CONFIG OVERRIDE: points the engine at Mechet's own cow husbandry XML so the
         C++ side loads the 30-entry animals[] array (vs RLRM bundle's 21 entries).
         This is necessary because i3d files cannot be reached from inside RLRM
         (FS25 has no cross-mod path substitution). Side effect: RLRM's deliberate
         Hereford-via-Angus-mesh-with-tile pattern at idx 16-18 and Highland-shifted-
         to-19-21 layout breaks under Mechet's base-game-aligned layout. We repair
         this for the new pens via property overrides on Hereford (hide from buy
         menu) and Highland (remap to Mechet's 16/17/18 = native Highland models).

      2. NEW SUBTYPES: Adds four bull subtypes (BULL_CHAROLAISE / BULL_MONTBELIARDE /
         BULL_SIMMENTAL / BULL_VOSGIENNE) for full RLRM reproduction.

      3. PROPERTY OVERRIDES on the four new cow subtypes:
         a. Modernised milk curve - 3-stage 7-key shape scaled to author's bumped peak.
            Author admitted in source comments (`valeur realiste = X` at lines 651/735/
            819) that milk peaks are bumped above realism for game balance; we keep
            those peaks and apply RLRM's 3-stage modernisation.
         b. RLRM universal cattle transportPrice 40/100/200 (vs Mechet's 50/80/100
            signature) - cattle modernisation consistency.
         c. Charolaise gets RLRM's modest beef-breed milk curve 0/0/190/190/265/265/125
            even though source has none - per project_rl_beef_cattle_milk_intentional
            memory and Witcombe Hereford precedent.
         d. Author's calf and adult input values for water/food/straw/manure/
            liquidManure are PRESERVED VERBATIM - the deliberately low calf inputs
            are a breed-character signature.
         e. Reproduction modernised to RLRM universal cattle maturity gate
            (minAgeMonth=12) on all four cows + bulls, matching the bundle
            pattern (every RLRM-bundled cattle subtype uses 12m) and the
            Witcombe precedent. Heritage gestation values from the source
            ARE preserved (durationMonth: Charolaise 14m, Simmental 9m
            heritage shorter, Montbeliarde 10m, Vosgienne 10m) so first-calf
            timing still differentiates the breeds: Charolaise 26m
            (slowest, heritage-paired), Simmental 21m (fastest, heritage),
            Montbeliarde and Vosgienne 22m (matches Holstein). Author's
            minHealthFactor preserved (Charolaise 0.80 heritage health gate,
            others 0.75).
         f. Author's buyPrice/sellPrice curves preserved verbatim - heritage premium
            signatures are signal-bearing.

      4. HEREFORD REGRESSION REPAIR (decision 1 = hide-on-Mechet): canBeBought=false
         on all four COW_HEREFORD/BULL_HEREFORD visual stages. Existing Hereford
         pens degrade visually but do not crash; no new Hereford appears in dealer.

      5. HIGHLAND VISUAL REMAP: COW_HIGHLAND_CATTLE/BULL_HIGHLAND_CATTLE point at
         Mechet's idx 16=baby / 17=kid / 18=adult (matches base-game Highland layout).
         RLRM bundle had Highland at 19/20/21; configOverride flipped these to
         Charolaise, so we remap.

    Property override rules (from RLMapBridge.applyPropertyOverrides):
      - Only explicitly defined properties are overridden (omitted = keep current value)
      - Works for both type-level and subtype-level properties
      - Same XML structure as animals.xml - no special tags needed
-->
<animals>

    <!-- Breed display names + marker colours for in-pen breed marker tags. -->
    <breeds>
        <breed name="CHAROLAISE"   displayName="$l10n_breed_charolaise"   markerColour="0.92 0.88 0.78"/>
        <breed name="MONTBELIARDE" displayName="$l10n_breed_montbeliarde" markerColour="0.78 0.55 0.42"/>
        <breed name="SIMMENTAL"    displayName="$l10n_breed_simmental"    markerColour="0.85 0.65 0.45"/>
        <breed name="VOSGIENNE"    displayName="$l10n_breed_vosgienne"    markerColour="0.45 0.45 0.45"/>
    </breeds>

    <!-- Replace COW configFilename with Mechet's 30-entry husbandry config so the
         engine loads the four custom breed models at indices 19-30. Path is
         relative to the map mod directory (g_modNameToDirectory["FS25_The_Mechet"])
         per RLMapBridge.loadConfigOverrides. -->
    <configOverrides>
        <override type="COW" configFilename="maps/animals/cow/animals.xml"/>
    </configOverrides>

    <animal type="COW">

        <!-- ======================================================================
             COW_CHAROLAISE: heavy French beef breed.
             Author intent: BEEF (no milk in source), heritage premium pricing,
             longer 14m gestation, earlier 15m maturity, higher 0.80 health gate,
             heavy inputs, big outputs.
             RLRM modernisation: milk curve added per beef-breed convention
             (0/0/190/190/265/265/125), transportPrice modernised to 40/100/200,
             reproduction.minAgeMonth modernised to 12 (universal RLRM cattle gate).
             Author signatures preserved: durationMonth=14 (heritage), minHealthFactor=0.80
             (heritage), buy/sell prices, all input curves, manure/liquidManure curves.
             First-calf timing: 12+14=26m (slowest of the four, heritage-paired).
             ====================================================================== -->
        <subType subType="COW_CHAROLAISE" breed="CHAROLAISE">
            <reproduction minAgeMonth="12"/>
            <transportPrice>
                <key ageMonth="0" value="40"/>
                <key ageMonth="12" value="100"/>
                <key ageMonth="18" value="200"/>
            </transportPrice>
            <output>
                <milk fillType="MILK">
                    <key ageMonth="0"   value="0"/>
                    <key ageMonth="12"  value="0"/>
                    <key ageMonth="12"  value="190"/>
                    <key ageMonth="36"  value="190"/>
                    <key ageMonth="36"  value="265"/>
                    <key ageMonth="72"  value="265"/>
                    <key ageMonth="120" value="125"/>
                </milk>
            </output>
        </subType>

        <!-- BULL_CHAROLAISE: heavy beef breeding-stock bull.
             Reproduction gate matches RLRM universal cattle maturity (minAgeMonth=12).
             Pricing 1.25x cow buy ratio (heritage premium). Sell shape 5-key with
             18m young-beef premium and 36m peak typical for heritage beef bulls.
             Transport: heavy-livestock 40/150/500. Adult input/output keyframes
             include small bull-side bumps (~+5-10%) over cow side; calf values
             mirror cow exactly per Witcombe BULL_HEREFORD pattern. -->
        <subType subType="BULL_CHAROLAISE" fillTypeName="BULL_CHAROLAISE"
                 gender="male" breed="CHAROLAISE"
                 minWeight="45.0" targetWeight="750.0" maxWeight="1400.0">
            <visuals>
                <visual minAge="0" visualAnimalIndex="19" name="$l10n_animal_visual_baby"
                        image="maps/animals/cow/store_cowCharolaiseBaby.png"
                        canBeBought="true">
